# Party-Axis

A nightlife event listing platform built for Singapore and the region. Promoters can submit events for review, and users can browse, filter, and discover what's on.

---

## Setting Up

You need Node.js installed on your machine before starting.

Clone the repo then go into the web folder:

```
cd Party-Axis/web
npm install
npm run dev
```

Then open http://localhost:3000 in your browser.

For the backend, set up a MySQL database using the schema in `api/schema.sql` and fill in your credentials in `api/config.php`. Set the `PARTYAXIS_BACKEND_URL` environment variable to point to your PHP deployment.

---

## Changes Made

- Replaced the color palette with a darker, easier on the eyes theme — less neon, more professional
- Fixed a password validation bug where the frontend and backend had different minimum length rules
- Signup form was collecting name, phone and city but never actually sending them to the server — fixed
- Publish form had all its validation working but was never submitting to the API — wired it up properly
- The "stay signed in" checkbox on login was being ignored — now sent to the backend
- City filter was cutting off at 10 cities with no way to see the rest — added a show more button
- Next.js version in package.json was set to 16.2.4 which doesn't exist — corrected to 15.2.4
- Event end time was in the database but never showing on cards — now displayed
- Added an event detail page at /events/[id] with the full info, map, and ticket link
- Added a user dashboard at /dashboard to see your submitted listings and their status
- Added WhatsApp and copy link share buttons on event cards
- Replaced the weekend-only filter with a proper date range picker
- Google Maps embed on the event detail page using the stored address
- Email goes out to the promoter when their listing gets approved or rejected
- Added a 404 page so broken URLs don't crash the app
- Publish form now disables and shows a loading state while submitting
